    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i cant go to hr about this. if they actually installed something like this, they'd just deny it and make me look crazy. im not looking for a policy manual, i'm looking for ways to protect myself. like, if there are sensors in the seat or backrest, can i do something physical to scramble the signal? like, would wearing specific clothes or using a certain type of cushion block the biometric readings?",
