      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Attempting to physically interfere with integrated sensors in a piece of furniture is unlikely to completely or reliably block biometric data transmission. Highly sensitive sensors can pick up signals through various materials, meaning simple clothing or cushions may not be an effective shield. You might consider using a physical blocker placed between your body and the chair's sensor points, though this is speculative and may void any warranties. Given the risk, changing your setup to a known private location or solely using that chair when entirely alone might be the safest short-term precaution.",
